<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Morlaix</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Morlaix is a port town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finistere">Finistère</a>, north-western Brittany, at the head of a long estuary opening onto the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">English Channel</a>. In the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and early modern period it prospered from the trade in linen cloth with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, and in 1522 it was sacked by an English raid. A large railway viaduct, built in the 1860s, dominates the town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/morlaix.jpg" alt="Morlaix" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thesupermat · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vue_de_Morlaix.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
